---
title: Tandoori Chicken
servings: 4
course: Main
locale: en_GB
prep time: 30m
cook time: 35m
difficulty: Medium
cuisine: Indian
tags:
- indian
- poultry
- savoury
- main-course
---

Remove any skin from the @chicken{6%pieces}(bone-in thighs, drumsticks, breasts, all skinless), and cut a couple of deep slashes in each piece.

Peel the @ginger{1%tbsp}(grated) and @garlic{6%cloves}(peeled), and blend into a paste with the @salt{1%tsp}. Stir in the @lemon or lime juice, or vinegar{6%tbsp}. Rub this mix over the chicken and leave for ~{30%minutes}.

Meanwhile, toast the @cumin seeds{1%tsp} in a dry pan until aromatic. Finely chop the @green chillies{2}(finely chopped). Blend the cumin, chilli, @garam masala{4%tsp}, @black pepper{}, and @Greek yoghurt{250%g}.

Smear the @paprika{2%tbsp} all over the chicken, followed by the yoghurt, rubbing it deep into the cuts. Cover and chill for 4 to ~{6%hours}. Take the chicken out of the fridge ~{30%minutes} before cooking.

Preheat the oven to 230°C. Grease a #baking tray{} with @ghee or oil{2%tbsp} and add the chicken pieces. Roast for ~{15%minutes}. Turn over the chicken pieces and cook for a further 10 to ~{15%minutes}.